              "body": "{\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-b0a63c4c-ccf9-4fbe-9352-8dd3d59dd01c\",\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": {\n        \"content\": \"A large language model is trained mainly to predict the next token based on massive amounts of text, capturing statistical patterns and fluent language generation. A reasoning model, by contrast, is structured (or fine‑tuned) to perform explicit multi‑step inference or logical operations, often building on an LLM’s knowledge but adding mechanisms—such as chain‑of‑thought prompting, symbolic modules, or neural planning layers—to solve problems that require step‑by‑step reasoning.\",\n        \"reasoning\": \"We need to answer in two sentences. The user asks: \\\"In two sentences, what is the difference between a large language model and a reasoning model?\\\" Provide concise description: Large language model: primarily trained to predict next token from massive text, capturing statistical patterns. Reasoning model: explicitly designed to perform logical or multi-step inference, often built on top of LLMs or separate architecture. Two sentences only. Let's craft clear answer.\",\n        \"role\": \"assistant\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created\": 1792260099,\n  \"model\": \"gpt-oss-120b\",\n  \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_a9089f3cce52797e7952\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"total_tokens\": 277,\n    \"completion_tokens\": 192,\n    \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n      \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\n      \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0,\n      \"reasoning_tokens\": 88\n    },\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 85,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n      \"cached_tokens\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  \"time_info\": {\n    \"created\": 1792260099.6181493,\n    \"queue_time\": 0.003085694,\n    \"prompt_time\": 0.001535216,\n    \"completion_time\": 0.101818774,\n    \"total_time\": 0.1107790470123291\n  }\n}",
